    {
      "id": "2",
      "volumeKey": "page-2",
      "label": "Page 2",
      "document": {
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "From backstage: Julie and Iain reveals their stories from rehearsal for"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-ee94a07ea834bb47"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Writer: Olsen, Journalist for"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Belobog Weekly"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-3bfd24f63f26b558"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"I've worked with Iain many times, but I still get nervous when I'm acting across him... There's a glimmer in his eyes, and I'm always sort of in a trance when looking at him.\" On the press night of"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", Julie revealed to the reporters present an interesting story during the rehearsal of"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-f022355707b5548d"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Julie and Iain both won the Goliards Award for Best Actor and Actress with their performance in"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Theater Story"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "last year. A month after winning the award, the two received an invitation from Amy, the playwright of"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ". Despite this stage couple of the drama world having already worked together many times before, Julie said with a smile that she still couldn't resist the unique charm of her old colleague."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-305e2420d063392b"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "is co-directed by two Goliards Award winners for Best Direction of a Play, and is romance novelist Amy's first stage play. Iain felt it was a little different from the typical romances, not just because it was co-directed by two well-known directors, but also because \"I felt amazing chemistry with Julie during rehearsals.\""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-788e0ec43d297aaa"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Iain tells us that during one rehearsal, Julie's skirt got tangled in a nearby prop. But because of the strong rapport between them — thanks to their countless past collaborations — Iain immediately caught Julie, and within the short duration of the changing backdrops, was able to help untangle her skirt."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-32ddaf9ddfd3df39"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Julie revealed that in this sudden incident, catching her was considered by director Jeffrey to be a \"stroke of genius,\" which happened to perfectly fit the scene of the botanist played by Julie being trapped: \"Alice is a botanist who is completely immersed into her career as a researcher. She is a little out of touch with the rest of society, so she doesn't know how to call for help, even when she's in a tight spot.\" \"But Howard's actions come from the heart.\" Taking this into consideration, Iain told us that because of this incident, this stage direction was written into the official script."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-236ba3a8ce88b063"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "\"Throughout the rehearsals of"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", we were infected with a wonderful atmosphere. While we had to perform in front of many people, as the plot developed toward the end, I think we must have entered a kind of blissful detachment, it felt really magical.\" Julie believes that"
              },
              {
                "type": "em",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stardust Rose"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "has a unique romantic atmosphere, different from all the plays she had acted in before. \"It's like being infected by love,\" Iain added."
              }
            ],
            "id": "p-7d66bef30a1c5b97"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
